    <solution><me>\mathbf{r}'(t)=\langle 2,-2,1\rangle</me>
and so
<me>||\mathbf{r}'(t)||=\sqrt{2^2+(-2)^2+1^2}=\sqrt{9}.</me>
The unit tangent vector is therefore:
<me>\mathbf{T}(t)
=\frac{\mathbf{r}'(t)}{||\mathbf{r}'(t)||}
= \frac{1}{\sqrt{9}}\langle 2,-2,1\rangle
=\left\langle \frac{2}{\sqrt{9}}, \frac{-2}{\sqrt{9}}, \frac{1}{\sqrt{9}} \right\rangle.</me>
We see that the unit tangent is constant, since the curve is a straight line.


</solution>
